==Walkthrough==
Speak to at least one expert of your [[character]]'s profession. They will teach you some skills. Return to First Spear Dehvad. He will teach you all the other skills the experts offer for your profession, so you do not have to speak to all of them. 

==Dialogue==
===Initial dialogue===
;First Spear Dehvad
:''"Ahai, <character name>! I heard about the role you played in saving Chahbek Village. Lady luck must have been smiling on you, eh? Well, now that the heroics are over, it's time you got back to your schooling. We've set up a temporary '''encampment''' nearby where our most skilled members have gathered to train recruits and help rebuild the village. Being a Sunspear is a lot like playing cards. It never hurts to learn a new trick or two!''

:''Would you like to go speak to an '''Expert <Profession>''' at the encampment?"''
{{offer dialog
|accept = It couldn't hurt to learn some new skills
|decline = I know everything I need to know.
|ask = As I said, you might learn a thing or two if you spoke to an '''expert''' at the '''encampment''' near Chahbek Village. }}

===Reward dialogue===
;First Spear Dehvad
:''"Did you learn a few things? Well, that's what school is all about. If you ever need to practice, head back to the encampment. I'm sure nobody would mind having a <Profession> of your caliber around.

:''Oh, I noticed you haven't chosen a secondary profession yet. Talk to me after you've gotten a bit more experience and I'll tell you how to choose."''

==Notes==
{{anomaly|Accepting the reward as a Ranger teaches Pin Down, even though none of the expert rangers offer the skill.}}

